%I A398605 #4 Aug 18 2026 10:16:40
%S A398605 1,12,620,21893
%N A398605 a(n) is the number of solutions to the "sum equals product" riddle with n distinct prices v_j, i.e., find positive integers v_j, v_{j+1}>v_j such that 100^(n-1)*Sum_{k=1..n} v_k = Product_{k=1..n} v_k.
%C A398605 a(n) > 0 for n <= 42; a(n) = 0 for n > 269 (see A382547 for more information).
%F A398605 a(n) <= A382510(n).
%e A398605 a(2) = 12: only one of the A382510(2) = 13 solutions contains equal prices, i.e., [200, 200], whereas the other solutions have distinct prices.
%e A398605 a(3) = 620: two of the A382510(3) = 622 solutions contain prices that are not distinct, i.e., [150, 150, 240] and [75, 300, 300].
%Y A398605 Cf. A380887, A381619, A381620, A381621, A382510, A382547.
%K A398605 nonn,bref,hard,more
%O A398605 1,2
%A A398605 _Hugo Pfoertner_, Aug 18 2026
